# CafeShop Project Standards

## Architecture and Layering
- Keep strict 3-tier flow: UI -> Service -> Repository/EF Core; do not bypass services from UI.
- Use DI for all services/repositories; prefer constructor injection and clear interface contracts.
- Keep modules aligned with business domains: Products, Categories, Orders, Coupons, Users, Payments.

## Backend ASP.NET Core (C#)
- Prefer async end-to-end (`async/await`); avoid `.Result` and `.Wait()`.
- Validate all request models and return clear API/UI validation messages.
- Use DTOs between layers; never expose EF entities directly to client/UI.
- Centralize exception handling and structured logging (`ILogger`) in middleware/filter.
- Optimize EF Core queries (`AsNoTracking`, projection, pagination) for listing/report pages.

## Security and Payment
- Enforce authentication/authorization by role (`Admin`, `User`) for every protected endpoint/page.
- Hash passwords with bcrypt-compatible approach; never store plain text credentials.
- Validate all inputs and rely on parameterized EF Core queries to prevent SQL injection.
- For VNPAY flow, always verify checksum/signature in callback before updating order/payment status.

## Frontend and UI/UX
- Build mobile-first, responsive layouts with Flexbox/Grid and relative units (`rem`, `%`, `clamp()`).
- Keep styling maintainable: semantic naming (BEM or equivalent), minimal `!important`, reusable tokens/variables.
- Ensure accessibility: color contrast, visible focus state, readable typography, reduced-motion support.

## Code Quality
- Follow Clean Code naming (`PascalCase` for class/type, `camelCase` for variables).
- Add tests for critical flows: auth, order lifecycle, payment callback, role-based authorization.
- Preserve existing behavior for core statuses (`Pending`, `Processing`, `Completed`, `Cancelled`).

